## Prerequisites

### AWS Account Setup

- [ ] AWS account with IAM permissions for resource creation
- [ ] AWS CLI installed and configured
- [ ] Terraform >= 1.5.0 installed
- [ ] Target region selected: `{{target_region}}`

### Heroku Access

- [ ] Heroku CLI installed and authenticated
- [ ] Access to source application(s): {{heroku_apps_comma_separated}}
{{IF has_postgres}}- [ ] Database credentials (`heroku pg:credentials:url -a <app>`){{ENDIF}}
{{IF has_redis}}- [ ] Redis URL (`heroku redis:credentials -a <app>`){{ENDIF}}
{{IF has_kafka}}- [ ] Kafka details (`heroku kafka:info -a <app>`){{ENDIF}}

### Network / Application

- [ ] VPC and subnet configuration confirmed (see `terraform/`)
- [ ] Security group rules reviewed
- [ ] Application Docker image built and pushed to ECR
- [ ] Env vars mapped to Secrets Manager / Parameter Store
- [ ] Health check endpoints identified

{{IF needs_containerization}}
### Containerization Prerequisites

Your app uses Heroku buildpacks (no Dockerfile). Create one for Fargate. Common
Procfile -> Dockerfile patterns: Node (`node:20-alpine`), Python
(`python:3.12-slim` + gunicorn), Ruby (`ruby:3.3-slim` + puma), Go (multi-stage
`golang:1.22` -> alpine), Java (`eclipse-temurin:21-jre`). Key differences: set
`PORT` explicitly (Heroku injects it); Docker needs explicit COPY+install; no
slug-size limit but keep images small.
{{ENDIF}}

{{IF interim_cutover}}
### ⚠️ Platform Risk Advisory

> Heroku is in sustaining engineering (stability-and-support only). Your selected
> approach (database first, app stays on Heroku temporarily) is a BOUNDED interim
> phase. Target exit date: **{{target_exit_date}}**. Limit hybrid operation to
> weeks, not quarters.
{{ENDIF}}

