## Phase 2: Data Migration

{{IF has_postgres}}
### PostgreSQL Migration (Heroku Postgres -> {{pg_target}})

Run `./scripts/migrate-postgres.sh`, or manually `pg_dump -Fc --no-owner --no-acl`
from the source and `pg_restore` to the target. Verify with row-count comparison
(`SELECT SUM(n_live_tup) FROM pg_stat_user_tables`).

{{IF interim_cutover}}
#### Interim Database Exposure (Public RDS + TLS)

RDS is temporarily publicly accessible so Heroku dynos can reach it (password +
TLS protected). Set `rds.force_ssl = 1`, use the RDS CA bundle, and include
`?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=...` in `DATABASE_URL`. Inbound 5432 from
`0.0.0.0/0` is temporary. ⚠️ CRITICAL: after the app migrates off Heroku, set RDS
"Not publicly accessible" and remove the `0.0.0.0/0` rule.
{{ENDIF}}

{{IF migration_method_dms}}
#### Alternative: AWS DMS (large DBs)

⚠️ DMS CANNOT do continuous replication (CDC) with Heroku Postgres (no
`REPLICATION` role) — one-time bulk copy + final cutover only. Copy schema first
(`pg_dump --schema-only`), migration type "Migrate existing data", run
pre-migration assessment, then final cutover.
{{ENDIF}}
{{IF migration_method_bucardo}}
#### Alternative: Bucardo (near-zero downtime)

Trigger-based replication on a dedicated EC2 instance; initial full copy then
delta-push until cutover. No LOB support; migrate functions via
`pg_dump --schema-only`.
{{ENDIF}}
{{IF migration_method_wal_g}}
#### Alternative: WAL-G (large DBs, minimal downtime)

WAL-based replication via a dedicated EC2 + S3 archive; continuous catch-up with
a minimal final cutover window.
{{ENDIF}}

#### Heroku CLI Cutover Sequence

`heroku maintenance:on` -> `heroku pg:backups:capture` -> final migration/sync ->
verify -> `heroku config:set DATABASE_URL=...` -> `heroku maintenance:off` ->
verify. After full migration: `heroku addons:detach DATABASE` (destroy only once
all data is confirmed in AWS).
{{ENDIF}}

{{IF has_redis}}
### Redis Migration (Heroku Redis -> ElastiCache)

Run `./scripts/migrate-redis.sh`. Small (<1GB): key-by-key `DUMP`/`RESTORE`.
Large (>=1GB): `redis-cli --rdb` snapshot via S3. Verify `DBSIZE` matches.
{{ENDIF}}

{{IF has_kafka}}
### Kafka Migration (Heroku Kafka -> Amazon MSK)

Option A (recommended): recreate topics on MSK (matching partitions/replication),
repoint producers, replay via offset reset. Option B: MirrorMaker 2 for
zero-downtime with large backlogs. Verify topic list + message counts.
{{ENDIF}}
{{ENDIF}}

