## Phase 3: Application Deployment

Build + push the image to ECR, then `aws ecs update-service --force-new-deployment`.
Migrate config vars: `heroku config --json` -> Secrets Manager (sensitive) +
SSM Parameter Store (non-sensitive), referenced in the ECS task definition.

> ECS Express Mode (optional): a Heroku-like deploy experience over the same
> Fargate + ALB infra; no design changes needed; identical cost model.

---

## Phase 4: Verification

- [ ] App responds on ALB endpoint; health check returns 200
{{IF has_postgres}}- [ ] DB connectivity confirmed; row counts match source{{ENDIF}}
{{IF has_redis}}- [ ] Redis connectivity confirmed; key counts match source{{ENDIF}}
{{IF has_kafka}}- [ ] Kafka producers/consumers working; topic config matches{{ENDIF}}
- [ ] App test suite passes against AWS; CloudWatch logs/metrics healthy

---

## Phase 5: Cutover

DNS: point `{{app_domain}}` CNAME at `{{ALB_DNS_NAME}}` (low TTL before cutover).

### Post-Migration Lockdown

- [ ] Disable public access on RDS/Aurora ("Not publicly accessible")
- [ ] Remove any `0.0.0.0/0` inbound DB rules; allow VPC-internal only
- [ ] Confirm automated backups + private VPC connectivity

### Decommission Heroku

After 48–72h parallel running: `heroku ps:scale web=0 worker=0`, then
`heroku addons:destroy` / `heroku apps:destroy` when confident.

